{"kind":"article","seeAlsoSections":[{"generated":true,"title":"Getting Started","identifiers":["doc:\/\/com.pushwoosh.PushwooshiOS\/documentation\/PushwooshFramework\/QuickStart","doc:\/\/com.pushwoosh.PushwooshiOS\/documentation\/PushwooshFramework\/GettingStarted"]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/com.pushwoosh.PushwooshiOS\/documentation\/PushwooshFramework\/AdvancedIntegration","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Article","title":"Advanced Integration Guide","modules":[{"name":"PushwooshFramework"}],"role":"article"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/com.pushwoosh.PushwooshiOS\/documentation\/PushwooshFramework"]]},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"abstract":[{"text":"Advanced configuration options for Pushwoosh iOS SDK integration.","type":"text"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This guide covers advanced configuration options including the delivery event, user identity, language and locale, In-App events, the push primer, feature flags, background modes, foreground notifications, logging, custom delegates, lazy initialization, and Info.plist properties."}]},{"level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Delivery-Event","text":"Delivery Event"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The message delivery event ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"messageDeliveryEvent"},{"type":"text","text":") is sent by the Notification Service Extension, a subclass of "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.pushwoosh.PushwooshiOS\/documentation\/PushwooshFramework\/PushwooshNotificationServiceExtension"},{"text":", when iOS hands it the push, whether the app is running or not. The app never sends this event: an integration without the extension has no delivery statistics. The extension and an App Group shared with the app are required; see step 4 of ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.pushwoosh.PushwooshiOS\/documentation\/PushwooshFramework\/QuickStart"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"text":"How the Event Is Sent","type":"heading","anchor":"How-the-Event-Is-Sent","level":3},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Push with a ","type":"text"},{"code":"pw_delivery_delay","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" window, App Group set."}]},{"type":"text","text":" The extension hands the event to iOS, which sends it at a random moment within the window (up to 300 seconds), so the notification is shown without waiting for the request. A failed attempt (no response, HTTP 408, 429, 500, 502, 503 or 504) is sent again 10 seconds × attempt number later, five attempts in all: by the extension while it runs, otherwise by the app, which iOS wakes in the background for it. The SDK takes these background session events in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"application(_:handleEventsForBackgroundURLSession:completionHandler:)"},{"type":"text","text":" itself; events of your own background sessions still reach your app delegate."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"No window, or no usable App Group."}]},{"text":" The extension sends the event at once, while it runs.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Incomplete configuration."}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" The event is skipped, and the extension logs what to configure:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":null,"code":["messageDeliveryEvent skipped: the Notification Service Extension has no Pushwoosh app code. Set Pushwoosh_APPID in the Info.plist of the app or the extension, or add the same App Group to both targets and set it as PW_APP_GROUPS_NAME in both Info.plist files.","messageDeliveryEvent skipped: the Notification Service Extension has no reverse proxy URL. Add the same App Group to the app and the extension targets and set it as PW_APP_GROUPS_NAME in both Info.plist files, so the extension reads the URL the app passes to setReverseProxy()."]},{"level":3,"anchor":"What-the-App-Group-Carries","type":"heading","text":"What the App Group Carries"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Add the App Groups capability with the same group to the app and the extension targets, and set the group as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PW_APP_GROUPS_NAME"},{"type":"text","text":" in both "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Info.plist"},{"type":"text","text":" files. Through it the extension gets:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"the delivery event scheduled for a "},{"code":"pw_delivery_delay","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" window, and its retries;","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"the reverse proxy URL passed to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Pushwoosh.configure.setReverseProxy(_:headers:)"},{"type":"text","text":". With "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Pushwoosh_ALLOW_REVERSE_PROXY"},{"text":" enabled and no App Group, the extension has no proxy URL and skips the delivery event rather than bypass the proxy;","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"the application selected at runtime with ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Pushwoosh.configure.setAppCode(_:baseUrl:)"},{"type":"text","text":". Without the App Group the extension reports deliveries to the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Info.plist"},{"type":"text","text":" application;"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"the badge count. The extension applies "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"pw_badge"},{"text":" (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"5"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"+1"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"-1"},{"type":"text","text":") only when the App Group is set, so increments add up across pushes."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Pushwoosh_APPID"},{"text":" and the other ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Pushwoosh_*"},{"type":"text","text":" keys do not need to be repeated in the extension’s "},{"code":"Info.plist","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":": the extension inherits them from the app. A value set in the extension overrides the app’s.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"To set the App Group in code instead of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Info.plist"},{"type":"text","text":", override "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.pushwoosh.PushwooshiOS\/documentation\/PushwooshFramework\/PushwooshNotificationServiceExtension\/pushwooshAppGroupsName()","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" in the extension."}]},{"text":"Integration Check","anchor":"Integration-Check","level":3,"type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"At every launch the SDK runs an integration check and prints the report to the console. It flags a missing Notification Service Extension, a "},{"code":"PW_APP_GROUPS_NAME","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" group the app has no App Groups capability for (checked on a device, not in the simulator), and different ","type":"text"},{"code":"PW_APP_GROUPS_NAME","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"code":"Pushwoosh_APPID","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" values in the app and the extension. Set "},{"code":"Pushwoosh_DISABLE_INTEGRATION_CHECK","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"YES"},{"text":" to turn the check off.","type":"text"}]},{"text":"User Identity","anchor":"User-Identity","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"Pushwoosh.configure.setUserId(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" attributes the device to your user, and ","type":"text"},{"code":"resetUserId()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" returns it to the HWID on logout or account deletion. "},{"code":"setUserId(\"\")","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" does not reset the user: an empty value is ignored.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"tabNavigator","tabs":[{"title":"Swift","content":[{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["func handleLogin(userId: String, email: String) {","    Pushwoosh.configure.setUserId(userId)","    Pushwoosh.configure.setEmail(email)","}","","func handleLogout() {","    Pushwoosh.configure.resetUserId()","    Pushwoosh.configure.setTags([\"logged_in\": false])","}"]}]},{"title":"Objective-C","content":[{"code":["[[Pushwoosh configure] setUserId:@\"user_123\"];","[[Pushwoosh configure] resetUserId];"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"objc"}]}]},{"anchor":"Language-and-Locale","level":2,"text":"Language and Locale","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"setLanguage(_:)"},{"text":" takes a two-letter ISO-639-1 code; ","type":"text"},{"code":"setLocale(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" takes a full BCP 47 tag such as "},{"code":"pt-BR","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"zh-Hant-TW"},{"type":"text","text":". The two are independent: an app that sets its own language should set the locale too, otherwise the device locale is reported. A new value is sent right away once the device has a push token; pass "},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" to return to the device value.","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","code":["Pushwoosh.configure.setLanguage(\"pt\")","Pushwoosh.configure.setLocale(\"pt-BR\")"],"type":"codeListing"},{"type":"heading","text":"Events and In-App Messages","level":2,"anchor":"Events-and-In-App-Messages"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Post events that trigger In-App Messages, reload In-App resources, and expose native methods to In-App HTML:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["Pushwoosh.configure.postEvent(\"productOpened\", withAttributes: [\"productId\": \"42\"])","","Pushwoosh.configure.reloadInApps { error in","    print(error == nil ? \"In-Apps reloaded\" : \"Reload failed\")","}","","final class JavaScriptInterface: NSObject, PWJavaScriptInterface {","    @objc func nativeCall(_ str: String, _ callback: PWJavaScriptCallback) {","        callback.execute(withParam: str)","    }","}","","Pushwoosh.configure.addJavascriptInterface(JavaScriptInterface(), withName: \"native\")"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"level":2,"anchor":"Push-Primer","type":"heading","text":"Push Primer"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A soft in-app dialog shown before the system permission prompt. The SDK checks the current authorization status, shows or skips the dialog, and registers for pushes when the user accepts:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["Pushwoosh.configure.pushPrimer","    .title(\"Stay in the loop\")","    .message(\"Get notified about deals first\")","    .acceptButton(\"Enable\")","    .declineButton(\"Later\")","    .present { outcome in }"]},{"type":"heading","text":"Feature Flags","anchor":"Feature-Flags","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Pushwoosh evaluates feature flags on the server; the SDK caches the last response and refreshes it by itself. "},{"code":"get","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" returns ","type":"text"},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" until the first response arrives. Call ","type":"text"},{"code":"logImpression","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" when the user sees a branch of the feature, including the disabled one:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","code":["let flags = Pushwoosh.configure.featureFlags","if flags.isEnabled(\"new_checkout\", default: false) {","    showNewCheckout()","} else {","    showOldCheckout()","}","flags.logImpression(\"new_checkout\")"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Background Modes","anchor":"Background-Modes"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"By default, iOS does not allow apps to process push notifications when they are in the background. To enable silent push notifications and background processing, you must enable Background Modes."}]},{"text":"Enable Background Modes in Xcode","level":3,"type":"heading","anchor":"Enable-Background-Modes-in-Xcode"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Open your Xcode project"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Select your app target"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Navigate to "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Signing & Capabilities"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" tab","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Click ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"+ Capability"}]}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Select ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Background Modes","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Enable ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Remote notifications","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" checkbox"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"orderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"This allows your app to:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Process silent push notifications in the background","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Update content when push notifications arrive","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Wake up the app to perform tasks"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Foreground Notifications","anchor":"Foreground-Notifications"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"By default, the SDK displays notification banners while the app is running in the foreground. You can control this behavior programmatically.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Control-Foreground-Alert-Display","text":"Control Foreground Alert Display","level":3},{"tabs":[{"content":[{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["\/\/ Enable foreground notifications","Pushwoosh.configure.setShowPushnotificationAlert(true)","","\/\/ Disable foreground notifications","Pushwoosh.configure.setShowPushnotificationAlert(false)"]}],"title":"Swift"},{"content":[{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"objc","code":["\/\/ Enable foreground notifications","[Pushwoosh.configure setShowPushnotificationAlert:YES];","","\/\/ Disable foreground notifications","[Pushwoosh.configure setShowPushnotificationAlert:NO];"]}],"title":"Objective-C"}],"type":"tabNavigator"},{"anchor":"Logging","type":"heading","text":"Logging","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The SDK provides multiple logging levels to help debug integration issues and monitor SDK behavior."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Available Log Levels","level":3,"type":"heading","anchor":"Available-Log-Levels"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"NONE","type":"text"}]},{"text":" - No logging","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"ERROR","type":"text"}]},{"text":" - Only errors","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"WARNING"}]},{"type":"text","text":" - Errors and warnings"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"INFO"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" - Default level, informational messages","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"DEBUG"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" - Detailed debug information"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"VERBOSE"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" - All possible logging","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"anchor":"Configure-Logging-via-Infoplist","text":"Configure Logging via Info.plist","level":3,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Add the following key to your "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Info.plist"},{"type":"text","text":":"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"xml","code":["<key>Pushwoosh_LOG_LEVEL<\/key>","<string>DEBUG<\/string>"],"type":"codeListing"},{"text":"Configure Logging Programmatically","level":3,"type":"heading","anchor":"Configure-Logging-Programmatically"},{"tabs":[{"title":"Swift","content":[{"syntax":"swift","code":["Pushwoosh.debug.setLogLevel(.PW_LL_DEBUG)"],"type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Available log levels:"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":".PW_LL_NONE"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":".PW_LL_ERROR"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":".PW_LL_WARN"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":".PW_LL_INFO"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":".PW_LL_DEBUG","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":".PW_LL_VERBOSE","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]}]},{"title":"Objective-C","content":[{"syntax":"objc","code":["[Pushwoosh.debug setLogLevel:PW_LL_DEBUG];"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Available log levels:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PW_LL_NONE"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"PW_LL_ERROR","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PW_LL_WARN"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PW_LL_INFO"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"PW_LL_DEBUG","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"PW_LL_VERBOSE","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]}]}],"type":"tabNavigator"},{"level":2,"text":"Custom UNNotificationCenterDelegate","anchor":"Custom-UNNotificationCenterDelegate","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"If you need to implement custom notification handling alongside Pushwoosh, you can register additional delegates through the notification center delegate proxy.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Register-Custom-Delegate","text":"Register Custom Delegate","level":3},{"tabs":[{"content":[{"code":["Pushwoosh.configure.addNotificationCenterDelegate(myDelegate)"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"}],"title":"Swift"},{"content":[{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"objc","code":["[Pushwoosh.configure addNotificationCenterDelegate:myDelegate];"]}],"title":"Objective-C"}],"type":"tabNavigator"},{"level":3,"text":"Implement Delegate Methods","type":"heading","anchor":"Implement-Delegate-Methods"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Use ","type":"text"},{"code":"PWMessage.isPushwooshMessage()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" to check if the notification is from Pushwoosh and handle only non-Pushwoosh notifications in your custom delegate."}]},{"type":"tabNavigator","tabs":[{"title":"Swift","content":[{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["func userNotificationCenter(","    _ center: UNUserNotificationCenter,","    willPresent notification: UNNotification,","    withCompletionHandler completionHandler: @escaping (UNNotificationPresentationOptions) -> Void",") {","    \/\/ Only handle non-Pushwoosh notifications","    if !PWMessage.isPushwooshMessage(notification.request.content.userInfo) {","        completionHandler([.banner, .list, .sound])","    }","}","","func userNotificationCenter(","    _ center: UNUserNotificationCenter,","    didReceive response: UNNotificationResponse,","    withCompletionHandler completionHandler: @escaping () -> Void",") {","    \/\/ Only handle non-Pushwoosh notifications","    if !PWMessage.isPushwooshMessage(response.notification.request.content.userInfo) {","        \/\/ Handle your custom notification","        completionHandler()","    }","}"]}]},{"title":"Objective-C","content":[{"code":["- (void)userNotificationCenter:(UNUserNotificationCenter *)center","        willPresentNotification:(UNNotification *)notification","        withCompletionHandler:(void (^)(UNNotificationPresentationOptions))completionHandler {","    \/\/ Only handle non-Pushwoosh notifications","    if (![PWMessage isPushwooshMessage:notification.request.content.userInfo]) {","        completionHandler(UNNotificationPresentationOptionBanner | UNNotificationPresentationOptionList | UNNotificationPresentationOptionSound);","    }","}","","- (void)userNotificationCenter:(UNUserNotificationCenter *)center","        didReceiveNotificationResponse:(UNNotificationResponse *)response","        withCompletionHandler:(void (^)(void))completionHandler {","    \/\/ Only handle non-Pushwoosh notifications","    if (![PWMessage isPushwooshMessage:response.notification.request.content.userInfo]) {","        \/\/ Handle your custom notification","        completionHandler();","    }","}"],"syntax":"objc","type":"codeListing"}]}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Lazy-Initialization","level":2,"text":"Lazy Initialization"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"By default, the Pushwoosh SDK initializes automatically when the app launches. Lazy initialization allows you to delay SDK startup until explicitly called."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"This is useful when:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"You need to obtain user consent before initializing the SDK"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"You want conditional initialization based on user preferences"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"You need to configure settings before SDK starts"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"anchor":"Enable-Lazy-Initialization","text":"Enable Lazy Initialization"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Add the following key to your "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Info.plist"},{"text":":","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"xml","code":["<key>Pushwoosh_LAZY_INITIALIZATION<\/key>","<true\/>"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"With this flag enabled, the SDK will not start automatically. Services will only activate when you explicitly call Pushwoosh SDK methods, such as:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"tabNavigator","tabs":[{"content":[{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["Pushwoosh.configure.registerForPushNotifications()"]}],"title":"Swift"},{"title":"Objective-C","content":[{"syntax":"objc","type":"codeListing","code":["[Pushwoosh.configure registerForPushNotifications];"]}]}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Info.plist Configuration Properties","anchor":"Infoplist-Configuration-Properties","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The SDK supports multiple configuration options through "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Info.plist"},{"type":"text","text":" keys."}]},{"level":3,"type":"heading","anchor":"Application-Configuration","text":"Application Configuration"},{"rows":[[[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Key","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Type","type":"text"}]}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Descr